  "claim": "Jean-François André Clervoy was the European Space Agency astronaut who participated in missions with NASA. An astronaut on a flight that engineer Daisuke Enomoto trained for did not.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Jean-François Clervoy. Sentence: Jean-François André Clervoy (born 19 November 1958) is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\nPage: Jean-François Clervoy. Sentence: He is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Thomas Reiter. Sentence: Thomas Arthur Reiter (born 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany) is a retired European astronaut and is a Brigadier General in the German Air Force currently working as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at the European Space Agency (ESA).\nPage: Expedition 14. Sentence: They joined Thomas Reiter, who had arrived at the ISS on 6 July 2006 aboard Space Shuttle \"Discovery\" during mission STS-121.\nPage: Daisuke Enomoto. Sentence: He had trained at Star City, Moscow in Russia to fly with two members of Expedition 14 on board Soyuz TMA-9, which was launched on September 18, 2006.",
