        "original_id": "0bf9be1b-1892-5366-a822-809c183be198",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-François Clervoy, Thomas Reiter, Daisuke Enomoto\n- Organizations: CNES, ESA, NASA, German Air Force\n- Roles: astronaut, engineer, Brigadier General, ESA Interagency Coordinator, Advisor to the Director General\n- Missions: Space Shuttle missions, STS-121, Expedition 14, Soyuz TMA-9\n- Places: Frankfurt, West Germany, ISS, Star City, Moscow, Russia\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-François André Clervoy was born on 19 November 1958.\n- Thomas Arthur Reiter was born on 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Thomas Reiter is a retired European astronaut and a Brigadier General in the German Air Force.\n- Thomas Reiter currently works as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at ESA.\n- Thomas Reiter arrived at the ISS on 6 July 2006 aboard Space Shuttle Discovery during mission STS-121.\n- Daisuke Enomoto trained at Star City in Moscow, Russia, to fly with two members of Expedition 14 aboard Soyuz TMA-9.\n- Soyuz TMA-9 was launched on 18 September 2006.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "772bae70-160d-5b0a-94a1-27181cab8749",
        "text": "Page: Jean-François Clervoy. Sentence: Jean-François André Clervoy (born 19 November 1958) is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\nPage: Jean-François Clervoy. Sentence: He is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Thomas Reiter. Sentence: Thomas Arthur Reiter (born 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany) is a retired European astronaut and is a Brigadier General in the German Air Force currently working as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at the European Space Agency (ESA).\nPage: Expedition 14. Sentence: They joined Thomas Reiter, who had arrived at the ISS on 6 July 2006 aboard Space Shuttle \"Discovery\" during mission STS-121.\nPage: Daisuke Enomoto. Sentence: He had trained at Star City, Moscow in Russia to fly with two members of Expedition 14 on board Soyuz TMA-9, which was launched on September 18, 2006.",
